course: dictionary
lesson: 7218
title: Phonemes: the smallest sounds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A phoneme is the smallest sound in a word that can change its meaning. Say «cat» slowly and you hear three sounds: /c/, /a/ and /t/. «A phoneme is one sound in a word; a grapheme is the letter or letters that write that sound.» This is the key idea of today's lesson.
explain: Change one phoneme and you get a new word. Swap the /c/ in «cat» for /h/ and you get «hat». The sounds are tiny, but each one can change the meaning. Listen for the sound, not the spelling.
explain: Do not mix up sounds and letters. A phoneme is the sound, and a grapheme is the letter or letters that write it. «Ship» has three phonemes, sh-i-p, but sh uses two letters to make one sound. To segment a word means to split it into phonemes, and to blend means to join them back together.
fact: A phoneme is the smallest unit of sound in a language that can change the meaning of a word.
fact: «Cat» has three phonemes: /c/, /a/ and /t/.
fact: Changing /c/ to /h/ in «cat» gives «hat».
fact: English has about 44 phonemes but only 26 letters, so some sounds need more than one letter.
fact: To segment a word means to split it into its phonemes; to blend means to put the phonemes together to say the word.
exercise: How many phonemes are in «cat»? | 2 | 4 | *3 | 1
exercise: Change /c/ to /h/ in «cat». Which word do you get? | *hat | pig | cup | cot
exercise: What is the difference between a phoneme and a grapheme? | A grapheme is a sound and a phoneme is a letter | A phoneme is a whole word | *A phoneme is a sound, and a grapheme is the letter or letters that write it | They mean exactly the same thing
test: How many phonemes are in «ship»? | 4 | 1 | *3 | 2
test: What does it mean to blend phonemes? | Split a word into its sounds | *Join the sounds together to say the word | Write the word with a pen | Count the letters in a word
exam: Which word has four phonemes? | *stop | dog | cat | ship
